VALUES (4600093826010111, ARRAY['"[8 marks] Analyze a process or equipment problem involving Vessels operating at low temperature within “Pressure Vessels”. Explain the principles, justify the selected method, and state a verification check and one limitation."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Analyze a process or equipment problem involving Design stress within “Pressure Vessels”. Explain the principles, justify the selected method, and state a verification check and one limitation."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Analyze a process or equipment problem involving Classification of reaction vessel within “Reaction Vessels”. Explain the principles, justify the selected method, and state a verification check and one limitation."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Analyze a process or equipment problem involving Design Consideration within “Design Consideration”. Explain the principles, justify the selected method, and state a verification check and one limitation."'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY[]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Pressure vessels contain pressurized fluids and require design consideration of pressure, temperature, materials, joints, corrosion and applicable codes.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order, connect it to Pressure Vessels; Operating conditions; Normal conditions; Transient conditions, and identify relevant process steps, equipment, variables or formulas. State assumptions and use consistent units where calculations apply.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete CHEMICAL PROCESS EQUIPMENT DESIGN process, equipment or design question within “Pressure Vessels”. State the expected outcome and why the selected method fits.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the outcome against the objective and note a source of error, safety concern or limitation.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/procedure 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1. Check technical details against official course material."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Pressure vessels contain pressurized fluids and require design consideration of pressure, temperature, materials, joints, corrosion and applicable codes.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order, connect it to Pressure Vessels; Operating conditions; Normal conditions; Transient conditions, and identify relevant process steps, equipment, variables or formulas. State assumptions and use consistent units where calculations apply.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete CHEMICAL PROCESS EQUIPMENT DESIGN process, equipment or design question within “Pressure Vessels”. State the expected outcome and why the selected method fits.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the outcome against the objective and note a source of error, safety concern or limitation.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/procedure 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1. Check technical details against official course material."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Classification of reaction vessel is listed under “Reaction Vessels” in the syllabus. Define it, explain its role and main process/design steps, relate it to Reaction Vessels, Material of construction, Heating system, Jackets, and apply it to a chemical-engineering operation or equipment decision. State relevant assumptions or variables and explain how to verify the result and one limitation.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order, connect it to Reaction Vessels; Material of construction; Heating system; Jackets, and identify relevant process steps, equipment, variables or formulas. State assumptions and use consistent units where calculations apply.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete CHEMICAL PROCESS EQUIPMENT DESIGN process, equipment or design question within “Reaction Vessels”. State the expected outcome and why the selected method fits.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the outcome against the objective and note a source of error, safety concern or limitation.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/procedure 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1. Check technical details against official course material."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Design Consideration is listed under “Design Consideration” in the syllabus. Define it, explain its role and main process/design steps, relate it to Material selection, Corrosion prevention, Stresses created due to static and dynamic loads, Combined stresses and theories of failure, and apply it to a chemical-engineering operation or equipment decision. State relevant assumptions or variables and explain how to verify the result and one limitation.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order, connect it to Material selection; Corrosion prevention; Stresses created due to static and dynamic loads; Combined stresses and theories of failure, and identify relevant process steps, equipment, variables or formulas. State assumptions and use consistent units where calculations apply.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete CHEMICAL PROCESS EQUIPMENT DESIGN process, equipment or design question within “Design Consideration”. State the expected outcome and why the selected method fits.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the outcome against the objective and note a source of error, safety concern or limitation.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/procedure 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1. Check technical details against official course material."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

