VALUES (4600093826040111, ARRAY['"[8 marks] Analyze a realistic task involving What is Entrepreneurship? in Entrepreneurship Development. Explain the governing principle, justify your approach, and include a verification check and one limitation."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Analyze a realistic task involving Classification & Characteristics of Entrepreneur in Entrepreneurship Development. Explain the governing principle, justify your approach, and include a verification check and one limitation."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Analyze a realistic task involving Creativity and Risk taking. in Entrepreneurship Development. Explain the governing principle, justify your approach, and include a verification check and one limitation."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Analyze a realistic task involving Business Reforms in Entrepreneurship Development. Explain the governing principle, justify your approach, and include a verification check and one limitation."'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY[]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** An entrepreneur identifies an opportunity, assembles resources and manages uncertainty to create value. Success depends on customer needs, feasibility, execution, finance and adaptation.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to Classification & Characteristics of Entrepreneur; benefits and drawbacks of entreprenrship; Creativity and Risk taking.; Business Reforms. State relevant rules, components, assumptions or formulas and how they affect the outcome.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Entrepreneurship Development task. Identify the objective, describe the selected procedure and state the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the outcome against the objective, note one limitation or error source, and justify the choice.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** An entrepreneur identifies an opportunity, assembles resources and manages uncertainty to create value. Success depends on customer needs, feasibility, execution, finance and adaptation.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to What is Entrepreneurship?; benefits and drawbacks of entreprenrship; Creativity and Risk taking.; Business Reforms. State relevant rules, components, assumptions or formulas and how they affect the outcome.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Entrepreneurship Development task. Identify the objective, describe the selected procedure and state the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the outcome against the objective, note one limitation or error source, and justify the choice.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Risk management identifies uncertainty, estimates likelihood and impact, assigns owners and plans avoidance, mitigation or contingency responses.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to What is Entrepreneurship?; Classification & Characteristics of Entrepreneur; benefits and drawbacks of entreprenrship; Business Reforms. State relevant rules, components, assumptions or formulas and how they affect the outcome.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Entrepreneurship Development task. Identify the objective, describe the selected procedure and state the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the outcome against the objective, note one limitation or error source, and justify the choice.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Business Reforms is covered under the syllabus unit “Unit 1”. Define the concept, explain its role and main components or steps, connect it to What is Entrepreneurship?, Classification & Characteristics of Entrepreneur, benefits and drawbacks of entreprenrship, Creativity and Risk taking., provide a practical course-related example and state one validation check or limitation.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to What is Entrepreneurship?; Classification & Characteristics of Entrepreneur; benefits and drawbacks of entreprenrship; Creativity and Risk taking.. State relevant rules, components, assumptions or formulas and how they affect the outcome.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Entrepreneurship Development task. Identify the objective, describe the selected procedure and state the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the outcome against the objective, note one limitation or error source, and justify the choice.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

