VALUES (4600093826040135, ARRAY['"[8 marks] Analyze a realistic task involving What is Entrepreneurship? in Entrepreneurship Development. Explain the governing principle, justify your approach, and include a verification check and one limitation."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Analyze a realistic task involving How to measure cost of project in Entrepreneurship Development. Explain the governing principle, justify your approach, and include a verification check and one limitation."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Analyze a realistic task involving Classification & Characteristics of Entrepreneur in Entrepreneurship Development. Explain the governing principle, justify your approach, and include a verification check and one limitation."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Analyze a realistic task involving benefits and drawbacks of entreprenrship in Entrepreneurship Development. Explain the governing principle, justify your approach, and include a verification check and one limitation."'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY[]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** An entrepreneur identifies an opportunity, assembles resources and manages uncertainty to create value. Success depends on customer needs, feasibility, execution, finance and adaptation.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to Classification & Characteristics of Entrepreneur; benefits and drawbacks of entreprenrship; Creativity and Risk taking.; Business Reforms. State relevant rules, components, assumptions or formulas and how they affect the outcome.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Entrepreneurship Development task. Identify the objective, describe the selected procedure and state the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the outcome against the objective, note one limitation or error source, and justify the choice.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** How to measure cost of project is covered under the syllabus unit “Unit 3”. Define the concept, explain its role and main components or steps, connect it to Sources of Finance, Assessment of working capital, Profitability and Product costing, Break Even Analysis and Financial Ratios and Significance, provide a practical course-related example and state one validation check or limitation.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to Sources of Finance; Assessment of working capital; Profitability and Product costing; Break Even Analysis and Financial Ratios and Significance. State relevant rules, components, assumptions or formulas and how they affect the outcome.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Entrepreneurship Development task. Identify the objective, describe the selected procedure and state the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the outcome against the objective, note one limitation or error source, and justify the choice.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** An entrepreneur identifies an opportunity, assembles resources and manages uncertainty to create value. Success depends on customer needs, feasibility, execution, finance and adaptation.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to What is Entrepreneurship?; benefits and drawbacks of entreprenrship; Creativity and Risk taking.; Business Reforms. State relevant rules, components, assumptions or formulas and how they affect the outcome.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Entrepreneurship Development task. Identify the objective, describe the selected procedure and state the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the outcome against the objective, note one limitation or error source, and justify the choice.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** benefits and drawbacks of entreprenrship is covered under the syllabus unit “Unit 1”. Define the concept, explain its role and main components or steps, connect it to What is Entrepreneurship?, Classification & Characteristics of Entrepreneur, Creativity and Risk taking., Business Reforms, provide a practical course-related example and state one validation check or limitation.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to What is Entrepreneurship?; Classification & Characteristics of Entrepreneur; Creativity and Risk taking.; Business Reforms. State relevant rules, components, assumptions or formulas and how they affect the outcome.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Entrepreneurship Development task. Identify the objective, describe the selected procedure and state the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the outcome against the objective, note one limitation or error source, and justify the choice.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

